    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I've got a heifer here that just came out of a rumenotomy about 6 hours ago. Can you give me a step-by-step protocol for what I need to be watching for over the next few days, specifically regarding the incision site and diet? Also, what are the main signs of internal infection I should look out for? Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the incision site, monitor closely for excessive swelling, redness, foul discharge, or signs of dehiscence (opening). Keep the area clean and dry, and restrict her movement to aid healing. Regarding diet, start with easily digestible, non-abrasive feed and gradually increase fiber as she recovers. Watch carefully for signs of internal infection such as persistent fever, severe lethargy, abdominal distension, or foul-smelling feces.",
      "source": "target",
